Title: Nick and Me
Credit: Written by
Author: Author
Source: Adapted from the book "Nick and Me"
Draft date: 7/30/2026

FADE IN:

INT. FIFTH-FLOOR APARTMENT - DAY

A modest brick walk-up on Kirk Street, Milwaukee. PETER, late 20s, average build, messy brown hair, sits at a worn kitchen table. His mother, MA (OLIVIA), 60s, frail with cloudy eyes, stares at a game show on an old TV.

PETER (V.O.)
Big brother was mine. Nick was the guy everybody was scared of. He had a pair on him the size of steel wrecking balls.

The door bursts open. NICK, 30s, broad-shouldered, scarred face, reddish-brown hair unkempt, Viking-tough, steps in carrying grocery bags like they weigh nothing. He nods at Peter.

NICK
What’s Ma doin’ back in the bedroom at this time of day?

PETER
I don’t know, why?

NICK
You got to keep an eye on her. She shouldn’t be sleeping in the middle of the day like that. That’s how old people go downhill.

Peter nods, ashamed. Nick sets the bags down, eyes the TV.

NICK (CONT'D)
She listens to everything I say. But you... you’re here to watch her.

Peter looks away. Nick slaps his shoulder, hard but brotherly, and leaves.

PETER (V.O.)
He is a modern-day warrior. Nobody questions that guy.

EXT. PIZZERIA SIDEWALK - DAY

Peter locks his bike. A young woman, SIONA, early 30s, pale skin, short brown hair, intense light-blue eyes, backpack, fish necklace, trips on the curb and brushes into him.

PETER
Are you okay?

SIONA
Yes.

She brushes off her cheap black V-neck shirt. They stare. She speaks like cool water.

SIONA (CONT'D)
Sionna. Named after an Irish goddess. The River Shannon.

PETER
I work here. What is your name — wait, you said Sionna. That’s different.

She smiles faintly. Peter fumbles.

PETER (CONT'D)
If you want to go have a cup of coffee sometime, you can call me.

SIONA
No thanks on the pizza. But coffee... yes.

She writes her number on his hand. As she walks away she glances back over her shoulder, as if memorizing him.

PETER (V.O.)
It was like I “knew” her. She was intense. Like waves on the ocean I saw once as a kid. I didn’t want to move my feet. I just wanted her to cover me completely.

INT. FIFTH-FLOOR APARTMENT - NIGHT

Ma rummages through pill bottles lined on the counter, mumbling.

MA
I can’t find my pain pills. Did we go to church today? Did you see Mrs. Canasta there?

PETER
Ma, we don’t go to church anymore. Your pills are right in front of you.

Ma’s eyes go glassy, empty. Then she snaps back.

MA
Oh, right. I see them. I don’t know what got into me.

Peter watches, worried. He grabs his coat.

PETER (V.O.)
I had to get out. Chances are I would see Nick down at Joe’s.

INT. JOE'S BAR - NIGHT

Football on TV. Packers vs Bears. Nick slaps Peter on the back.

NICK
Hey, little brother. What’s shakin’?

PETER
Nothin’.

Peter tells him about Ma. Nick’s face darkens.

NICK
I knew she would start going crazy cooped up in that place all day. Why don’t you take her to the store or something? Holy Christ, do something with her before we have to pay for a nursing home.

Peter shrinks. Nick’s fists clench.

NICK (CONT'D)
That’s how old people go downhill. They take every last dime.

PETER
I just needed to get away for a while.

Nick gives him a look that could punch through walls. Peter pays for his beer.

PETER (V.O.)
God, sometimes I really hate Nick inside. But I would never tell anybody this.

EXT. LIBRARY - NIGHT

Peter slips inside instead of going home. The place smells of old wood and paper. He wanders to CLASSIC LITERATURE.

PETER (V.O.)
Who needed school when you could get the same thing for free?

He grabs WUTHERING HEIGHTS. Checks it out with a thin smile from the librarian.

INT. FIFTH-FLOOR APARTMENT - NIGHT

Peter reads by lamplight. Ma is already in bed. He flips pages about Heathcliff and Catherine.

PETER (V.O.)
It reminded me of Sionna. A love that never changes will destroy you.

He falls asleep. Dream sequence: Peter as a medieval rider in embroidered tunic on a horse with Sionna in linen dress, long hair, light-blue eyes. They kiss in a sunlit field. He wakes sweating.

PETER
Hold!

INT. JAVA HUT COFFEE SHOP - DAY

Peter and Sionna at a small table. Backpacks, textbooks. Her eyes are watery blue crayons.

SIONA
I read it. Wuthering Heights. The moors are like its people — wild, unpredictable. A love that never changes will destroy him.

Peter listens, rapt. Something awakens in him.

PETER
It reminded me of the way Nick is. Strong and unwavering. But somehow it seemed dumb.

SIONA
A love that never changes will destroy you.

They talk symbols, ghosts, double characters. Peter looks smarter just being near her.

PETER (V.O.)
She made me feel like I belonged somewhere. Like I really mattered.

They make a dinner date for Friday. As he leaves:

PETER (V.O.)
Maybe that was Ma’s problem all along. Dad left, and Ma never moved on. It just ended up destroying her.

INT. YOGA STUDIO - DAY

Peter, awkward in t-shirt and shorts, lies on a purple mat in corpse pose. Sionna beside him. The class ends. He feels calm, relaxed.

SIONA
You were really great at that.

PETER
Are you kidding me?

SIONA
Your practice is your practice. The only thing that matters is what’s going on on your mat.

They smile. Peter looks changed — less reactive.

INT. FIFTH-FLOOR APARTMENT - EVENING

Nick stomps in, red-faced. Ma looks upset.

NICK
Ma missed her doctor’s appointment yesterday, you ass. Where the hell were you?

PETER
I was with someone. I met a girl.

NICK
A girl. That’s worth all this? Try looking at your priorities, Bro.

Peter tries to explain. Nick’s fists clench. They argue louder.

PETER
You haven’t even met her. Give her a fuckin’ break!

NICK
Don’t you talk to me like that, you little bastard.

Nick slaps him across the head. Peter’s ear rings. Nick storms out, slamming the door.

PETER (V.O.)
I had never been in a screaming fight with Nick before. In that split second, I knew I never wanted Sionna to meet that prick.

INT. HOSPITAL ROOM - DAY

Ma in bed, monitors beeping. Peter sits by the window. Sionna visits for lunch; they walk outside briefly. Peter returns alone, falls asleep in the chair.

DREAM: Chaotic battlefield. Peter as soldier stands over a dying man who whispers “Save her.” Nick runs at him with a knife, stabs him in the chest.

NICK (DREAM)
That you are, little brother.

Peter wakes gasping. Ma dozes. Nurses explain her dementia, high blood pressure, nitro pills. Peter and Sionna later fill a weekly pill container.

PETER (V.O.)
For the first time in my life, things were starting to go right. I had a girlfriend that really liked me. My Ma liked her too.

INT. FIFTH-FLOOR APARTMENT - NIGHT

Nick visits. Ma is tucked in. Peter shows the pill container proudly.

NICK
Oh, holy shit! Aren’t you nurse Nancy!

Tension rises. Nick mocks Sionna. They scream.

PETER
You’re so Goddamn hateful. What the fuck got into you?

Nick slaps him again. Peter stands his ground.

PETER (V.O.)
Who needs Nick, really? Me and Ma and Sionna would be just fine without him.

INT. HOSPITAL EMERGENCY ROOM - NIGHT

Chaos. Officers and nurses. Peter arrives frantic. An OFFICER approaches.

OFFICER DUPUIS
Mr. Olson, there has been a serious accident. Your brother and mother were hit broadside. Your mother passed away at the scene. Your brother is in serious condition.

Peter collapses into a chair. Later, alone with Ma’s empty chair at home, he sobs.

PETER
Die you fucking jackass. Die.

Sionna arrives, holds him.

INT. SIONA'S DUPLEX - NIGHT

Peter bursts in. Nick has Sionna pinned to the wall, knife at her collarbone.

NICK
If I wanted to kill you, I could kill you right now. Break it off with him tonight or else.

Peter tackles Nick. Struggle. The knife plunges into Sionna’s shoulder. Blood. Nick flees. Peter presses the wound, dials 911.

PETER
Stay with me. Please.

Sionna’s eyes dim. Sirens approach.

INT. PRISON VISITATION BOOTH - DAY

Years later. PETER, now sharper, successful-looking, sits across thick plexiglass. NICK, older, graying, thinner, worn, picks up the phone on his side.

PETER
I’m here to tell you that even though you are my brother... I am no longer interested in seeing you. You killed my mother. You held me down my entire life. You tried to kill the love of my life.

Nick looks down, tears forming.

PETER (CONT'D)
But I forgive you, Nick. Because it sets me free.

NICK
I’m so sorry. I really am. You’re a big man. I’m a small one.

They stare. A guard signals time.

PETER
After all is said and done, I still love you for being my brother.

Nick is led away. Peter hangs up the phone, sits a moment, then stands. A weight lifts.

PETER (V.O.)
President Olson. That’s me.

FADE OUT.

THE END
